 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Precision**: The method relies on floating-point arithmetic. If $a_{under}$ is very close to zero, the quadratic formula may suffer from cancellation errors. A fallback to linear solving is recommended if $|a_{under}|$ is negligible [G].
-*   **Conservatism**: The underestimation is conservative. If the underestimated polynomial has roots, the original polynomial *might* still not have roots (false positive for intersection). However, if the underestimated polynomial has *no* roots, the original definitely has none (true negative for collision) [S1].
